――A roaring, skin-searingly cold wind enveloped the entire Great Glacier.

"――――"

Even bundled in thick winter gear, he could still feel the piercing cold of the air. He forced his vision, which threatened to cloud with white breaths, open and looked ahead.

If the only enemy were the cold, there would be plenty of ways to bundle up more. But the true enemy here wasn't the biting wind or snow.

It was a threat that pointed a far clearer blade at his very life.

"――Are you scared?"

Suddenly, hearing a voice ask that, he became aware of the feel of his partner's soft hand.

The warmth he felt in his continuously held left hand was that of the best partner, one filled with nothing but trust and affection, who would never abandon him no matter how dire the straits.

"Nah, besides, I could stuff this full of positive feelings like protectiveness, cuteness, passion... I'm running out of words to praise you, you know."

"Fufun, naturally. I'd love to hear those insufficient words as much as time allows, but... it seems we have some pests right now."

"Yeah. ――Man, I figured as much, but I wish they'd give us a break."

Agreeing with his cute partner, he shrugged, but his gaze remained forward – while they exchanged lighthearted banter, his vigilance, not slackening in the slightest, was fixed entirely on the being standing there.

Honestly, no matter how much tension or vigilance he poured out, it would never be enough against this opponent.

"I still wonder if it's valid to use you as a measuring stick, but... compared to how dangerous you are, Regulus is cute... no, that's not right. Regulus is more like a flea."

"――I shall take that as a special evaluation from you."

He closed one eye at the opponent who had caught his mutter with supernatural hearing and replied so punctually.

A relaxed standing posture, a tall, well-trained physique clad in splendid attire, a gaze that showed a will to carry through with terrifying resolve, and slightly sunburned-looking, swarthy skin. Faintly rising on that skin were tattoo-like, mysterious patterns resembling Sanskrit.

A man whose very appearance screamed he was no ordinary person – and indeed, he was anything but. ――At the very least, even looking across the entire world today, there was probably no one who could defeat him.

――Known as the 'Mad Prince'.

That was the formidable enemy they now faced on the Great Glacier, where an icy blizzard raged.

"'Facing,' huh. ...Why do we have to fight each other anyway?"

"A self-question? If it is a doubt, then one must doubt that doubtful attitude. As for the reason why, I believe I have exchanged many words with you. And after that, we reached an impasse. Hence this situation. ――It is hardly to my liking either."

"Hardly to your liking? Why's that?"

"I hold neither grudge nor hatred towards you. The reason you and I must face each other has nothing to do with like, dislike, or animosity. It is simply――"

Saying that, the 'Mad Prince' paused, narrowing his eyes and lowering his gaze slightly. This shift made it clear his focus had moved from the man himself to the partner beside him.

In that instant, a viscous, unceasing hatred oozed from the opponent.

That was certainly an emotion never directed at the man the 'Mad Prince' faced. And precisely for that reason, it was why he and that man could never see eye to eye.

Letting that undisguised hatred spill out, the 'Mad Prince' declared.

"――It is over that filth that you and I are irreconcilable."

"First of all, I can't understand that aesthetic sense of yours that calls my super cute partner 'filth.' That's why I can never be friends with you."

"Exceedingly regrettable. So regrettable, it is deeply regrettable. Regrettably, I will not back down."

The 'Mad Prince' slowly shook his head side to side, sighing as if lamenting the failure of persuasion. But if he had truly intended to persuade with that, then the chasm in their values would likely never be bridged.

"He really is impossible to talk to. ...I wonder if we could have talked more with Cecilus."

"Comparing him to Cessi makes me feel bad for Cessi. I could talk to Cessi just fine... it's just that the conclusion of the conversation would conveniently land wherever Cessi wanted it to. That's the logic of the strong, I guess."

"But we can't let them have their way. ――You should know that, right?"

"――Yeah, you don't have to tell me. Though being told does get me more pumped up."

He tightened his grip on their joined hands, exchanged a glance and a smile.

Before the showdown with the formidable enemy, their sense of unity with his partner was sufficient. ――And then, the reason they had chosen this place as their battlefield and spent so much time in dialogue suddenly came to mind.

It was at the edge of his vision, a prism of absolute ice that glinted for just a moment――,

"『――E・M・M!!』"

Instantly, their overlapping incantations activated, and the absolute defense magic enveloped him and his partner, shifting their existence half a step away from this world, nullifying all interference.

Passing through their blurred, insubstantial bodies, piercing through to the other side, was a white light that had ruthlessly aimed to blast out their knees. If they hadn't blocked it, the two standing side-by-side would have had their legs shot out together, surely rendering them combat-incapable.

And that same attack had also targeted the 'Mad Prince' – however――,

"――Is that your full power? Or do you wish to anger me? If this is provocation, be prepared to receive the retribution? The one who inflicts is I, the one who receives is you."

As he spoke, the 'Mad Prince' caught the white light between two raised fingers.

The light slowly lost its brilliance at the man's fingertips, eventually revealing the form of a single long needle, which then crumbled and dissipated into mist. ――That attack, which fired needles constructed from magic at super-high speed, was known as this:

"Hell's Snipe... that means――"

"――So it's you again? You never learn, do you? No matter how many times you come, it'll be the same."

"――――"

Suddenly, at the voice that fell from above, he involuntarily held his breath.

The wind still roared fiercely. And yet, why was it? Why, even within such a gale, did that voice so clearly reach his eardrums?

Perhaps the logic of the strong was a power that could subdue even the laws of nature and force them to obey.

If that were true, it made sense that her voice could cut through the blizzard to reach them.

After all, the being that now appeared calmly in the sky above the Great Glacier – she was――,

"――It has been a while, 'Witch of Melancholy.' Are you well?"

"Would you stop talking to me like we're acquaintances? I'm neither your friend nor your casual acquaintance. And you don't really care if I'm well or not, do you?"

"Not exactly, not exactly. After all, you and this man here are currently significant obstacles to my achieving my goal. If there were ever a time when you were unwell, I would very much like to take advantage of it."

"Oh, is that so? Then, if I spread a false rumor that I'm in terrible shape, would you come leaping in believing it? Wow~, go die."

Clapping her small hands lightly in front of her chest, the woman floating in that cold sky laughed cruelly.

"――――"

She was a beautiful woman.

Her long, reddish-brown hair was tied up with a ribbon, and she wore a dress with special patterns mixing multiple colors – pink, light blue, and gold.

Baring her white, slender shoulders, her outfit was unbelievably light for the frigid glacial region, but for her, whose breath didn't even turn white, it seemed to pose no obstacle at all.

Just as the sound of the blizzard could not drown out the beautiful tones that spilled from her lips, things like heat, cold, or inclement weather could not hinder her from doing what she wanted or wearing what she liked.

"――She's here."

That call brought back his consciousness, which had been frozen, breath held.

His partner, who must have been looking at the same opponent and reached the same state of mind, was still considerate of his feelings, desperately holding back her own overflowing emotions.

He didn't find that consideration pathetic, nor did he feel sorry for it. ――He simply took a deep breath, determined not to waste her kindness.

And then――,

"――We finally meet again, ■■■!"

"――――"

He called out loudly to her, there beyond the white, hazy wind.

Unfortunately, unlike her or the 'Mad Prince,' he had no way to overpower the wind.

Besides, having to take back the words of this moment, built up for so long, just because they didn't reach her – he absolutely did not want to do anything that lame.

Just how long had he waited for this moment?

How much helplessness had he savored, overcome, and trudged through to get here?

Seeking the fruition of all of it, he took a breath―― Natsuki Subaru stared at ■■■.

As he stared, he spoke.

"I'm going to get you back, ■■■. ――Bring it on, Destiny!!"

This was the culmination of the long time Natsuki Subaru had spent before setting foot on this frozen land, the very reason for that time, and a declaration serving as the settlement of the days he had decided to dedicate everything.




