――Dark. Dark. Dark. He continued to drift in a dark abyss.

Vague as a doze, uncertain as eternity, scattered as mire.

Like being forever on the border between the pages of dream and reality within a single book – he drifted through such a vague, uncertain, scattered, endless darkness.

Just how long had he been like this?

Just how much longer would he be like this?

Just how far would this endlessly continuing instant go?

The darkness stretched out even those thoughts, doubts, and propositions that should naturally exist.

Stretched thin, they became like flimsy tissue paper, easily torn with a slightly stronger poke, their connections lost, eventually losing their original shape.

Surely, he had repeated that many times now.

Gathering his dissipating consciousness, scraping it together, connecting it – only to easily shatter it again with a tiny application of force, scattering it back into pieces.

Perhaps he should just give up trying to hold together something that had broken so many times he'd lost count. ――And yet, he couldn't.

――Dark. Dark. Dark. He continued to drift in a dark abyss.

Vague as a doze, uncertain as eternity, scattered as mire – but never alone, he continued to drift in the darkness.

Not alone. He would not be alone.

The stretched-out instants, the repeated failures, the darkness he continued to drift in – the reason that he was not alone held them back, refusing to let them disappear.

Even though his own definition of self was incomplete, even though the proof of not being alone was shrouded in black mist – still, he could not give up, could not let go, could not abandon it.

He could not give up. ――Because giving up didn't suit him.

So――,

