"――――"

The moment his vision opened and he was thrown out into the outside world, his mind was violently churned by the flood of information that rushed in, and his body convulsed intensely.

"――Tch"

His vision flickered, the contrast of red and black alternately violating the world.

Tension shot through his outstretched limbs, and the overexertion of his body, now free of unconscious brakes, caused a terrifying sequence of cramps – from his fingertips to their roots, through the muscles of every joint in order.

Pain, pain that reached every corner of mind and body, seized him and wouldn't let go.

"I've burned it all awaaay!! And now, wha-wha-wha!? Is this okay, I wonder!? He looks like a fish washed ashore, don't you think!?"

"Be silent, Lumera. No matter how impossibly adorable your appearance may be, I don't recall allowing you to shriek in my ear. This is a natural result, is it not."

"Natural!? Your Excellency, did you just say natural? Did you know this would happen!?"

"My 'Sun Sword' burns what I wish to burn and cuts what I wish to cut. However, since I deployed it without following proper procedures, I cannot deny the possibility of complications."

"...Couldn't you have mentioned that earlier?"

"One should know such a trivial thing without being told. After all, you all are, without exception, older than I, who am wise yet still young. Or have you wasted your lives with your heads gathered together like that?"

Swallowed by the torrent of information captured by all five senses – sight, hearing, smell, taste, touch – his consciousness was forcibly stirred, and voices flew back and forth above him.

Those voices were also new information. In other words, part of the rushing torrent.

"This is bad, bad, bad! If he dies like this, years of hard work will be for nothing!? I ran all over, groveled on the ground so many times, finally made it here, and now... ugh, I won't be able to show my face to anyone!"

"This is no time for talk, you know! In times like these... yes, drastic measures! A little pain is elegant if it brings results! I'm sure Master would even smile and say 'well done,' don't you think!?"

"That's it! Can you do it, Miss Lumera!"

"Of course it's utterly impossible, I wonder! I am fire-aspected, burning bright after all! All fire can do is destruction, and the destruction part of destruction and regeneration, I wonder! Ohohohoho!"

"Is this maybe just a complete waste of time right now!?"

Panicked voices, exceptionally loud even within the flood and torrent, moved left and right.

Feeling the exchanges, sandwiching him, roaring back and forth, amidst the pain in mind and body, he became aware of a slowly approaching threat – the information known as difficulty breathing.

"――Gh"

His stomach walls convulsed, and the tube serving as his airway began to close due to internal contraction.

A tragedy caused by unnatural peristalsis of the body, but what awaited at its end was a comedy no one would laugh at. His body, already weakened by extreme depletion, was now losing function due to respiratory failure.

And yet, amidst the chaos of overwhelming information, he couldn't find a way to fix it.

"You lot, is it alright to be making such a racket? This fellow is on the verge of death. Since he is a man I have no acquaintance with, his death would not affect me in the slightest, but that is not the case for you, is it."

"Well, that's really, really true, but we've also poured in our resources until we're at our absolute limit, so we have no leeway! What if we put him back in that ball from earlier? No, that won't work, right? Yes!"

"He resolved that himself rather quickly. An entertaining fellow. ――Hmm, I see. Even with my radiance, there is little I can do for a dying clown... but this is different."

"What are you planning?"

"Fool, why do you look at me as if it's someone else's problem, 'Unryuu'? ――That man aside, there is something I can do for this dear girl, is there not."

Unable to cope, the suffering intensified, and intensified, and intensified.

That suffering, that pain, that convulsion painted over everything, and the instant that should have been stretched into eternity was now covered by a thick, heavy end.

At this rate――,

"――――"

――At this rate, was it the end?

"――Subaru!"

In that instant, another piece of information struck his consciousness, which had been about to close in darkness. But this time, it was not something that merely prolonged the pain and suffering.

It was something that wiped away pain with pain, suffering with suffering, information with information.

And then――,

"You mustn't die. You're not going to die, are you...!"

And that information, that suffering, that pain – it was something precious he knew well.

"――Ah"

The convulsing stomach walls, the closing throat, the tangled tongue, the flickering vision, the consciousness about to be swallowed by the instant, the life that should have scattered into the dark distance – all of it stopped.

Don't let go. Of anything. Don't throw away. Anything. Cling on. To the world.

He had to do that, he had to be able to do that, only by doing that――,

"Gh, ugh, ah"

"Subaru!"

The annoying flickering red and black light vanished, and he saw tearful eyes illuminated by the backlight.

Eyes with a characteristic butterfly-shaped pattern, a beloved voice calling his name, a small-bodied, great existence desperately holding onto his about-to-scatter being.

"Ah, yo..."

"――Yes, that's right. Isn't it? It's alright. I'm here, aren't I?"

With a body that wouldn't move anywhere, with a fragile, numb, battered heart – still, to prove himself, to tell her he remembered her, he forced out words.

She would receive them. Yes, as if crossing the bridge of trust with his eyes closed.

"No matter what happens, we can get through it, Subaru. Betty and the others, that is."

Holding those reliable, encouraging words close, his consciousness cut out.

――That was the event of the first day of Natsuki Subaru's resumption of his journey.


