When his eyelids faintly opened, the first thing that leaped into view was an unfamiliar ceiling.

"――Ghoh"

He tried to voice what he saw, but his bone-dry mouth and terribly ravaged throat wouldn't produce a proper sound, only allowing an ugly groan.

Like the death rattle of a crushed frog.

But――,

"――Are you awake? You're quite a sleepyhead, a bad child, you know."

That was enough to convey it to the one waiting by his bedside for his awakening.

His forehead, along with his bangs, was tickled by a small hand that reached out gently. Subaru, narrowing his eyes at the pleasant sensation, looked over to see a girl with softly lowered eyes – Beatrice – there.

Her unchanging form, her unchanging gaze, her unchanging warmth – she was there.

Unmistakably, without a single difference, Beatrice was there, just as seared into his consciousness.

"Ah, yo..."

"Yes, it's Betty, no mistake. Don't worry, so you mustn't push yourself. Right now, Subaru's heart and body have their wires crossed, making things terribly difficult, I suppose."

"Ha, uh..."

He hadn't intended to push himself to the point of being told he was pushing himself.

He simply wanted to sit up, scoop up Beatrice with his surging emotions, dash outside the room, and spin around together with her in a wide-open space.

But even that seemed too much to ask of Subaru right now. ――His heart and body had their wires crossed, as Beatrice had put it.

"――Gh"

In fact, it seemed true that Subaru's brain had forgotten how to move his body.

He could barely capture Beatrice at the edge of his unmoving eyeballs, which was why he could see her, but neither his fingers nor even his eyeballs would roll as Subaru wished.

It felt like a miracle not only to sit up, but even to be managing to breathe at all.

He supposed he should be grateful his heart hadn't forgotten how to beat.

"Quite frankly, it's no laughing matter. While you were sealed inside that place, apart from Betty, your life functions had almost completely ceased, I suppose. To the point where your body forgot how to do things that should be natural, you see."

"――Ah"

"That space... It was an incredible thing woven from a Yin Magic that Betty doesn't know, I suppose. Without a doubt, Mother had a hand in it. Why that man had mastered a forbidden technique created by Mother... the mysteries are endless, I suppose."

"――Ih"

"I have no intention of debating that with Subaru. No matter what Subaru might say, to Betty, Mother is Mother, an irreplaceable person, I suppose. Hmph, that's how it is."

What haltingly entered were only Subaru's interjections, nothing but raspy breaths.

Yet Beatrice, receiving them, held a conversation with exceptional understanding, and furthermore, while still touching Subaru's forehead, she puffed out her cheeks in dissatisfaction and turned her face away with a "Hmph."

Her expression, unable to lean entirely toward either affection or displeasure, was unbearably endearing――,

"...Are you really having a conversation there? To me, it looks like Beatrice-chan is just getting excited all by herself."

That voice, heard suddenly, belonged to a third party, neither Subaru nor Beatrice.

In his field of vision, Beatrice went "Mm" and looked toward Subaru's feet, so the owner of the voice seemed to be standing there. Unfortunately, Subaru had no means of looking that way.

To that person who wouldn't enter his view, Beatrice, still puffing her cheeks, said,

"Don't say such rude things. Besides, the bond between Subaru and Betty is infinite... Betty can tell what Subaru wants to say just by looking into his eyes, you know."

"I see, I see, so that's what it means to be a Spirit Arts User and their Contracted Spirit? I'm fairly surrounded by spirit-related people, but that part is hard for an outsider to grasp intuitively."

"Other cases aside, the relationship between Betty and Subaru is unique, I suppose. Well, every contracted spirit probably thinks the same about their partner, so it's for your own safety not to speak as if you know better."

"Right, thanks for the advice. Oh, and, could I offer my greetings soon as well?"

Saying that, the person beyond his feet seemed to have asked Beatrice for permission to greet him.

Beatrice, thus petitioned, sighed softly, then looked at Subaru with her large eyes. Asking if it was alright to let him greet her. Subaru nodded with his feelings.

"――Uh"

"I suppose I'll allow you to show your face. Be grateful, or so she says."

"Well, isn't that generous! You're just as sharp-tongued as I'd heard, my word!"

Saying that, the owner of the voice approached, thudding heavily across the floor.

Somehow, a familiar tone – but the voice itself he didn't recognize. He could only await the approach of such a person like a fish on a chopping board.

As Beatrice slowly drew back, in the cleared space of his vision, he saw the face of the person who popped into view.

It was a handsome, 'unfamiliar' young man with green-based clothing, a large hat, frizzy gray hair, and an androgynous facial expression――,

"Hello, nice to meet you, Natsuki Subaru-san. ――My name is Nicola Suwen. I have various titles, but 'merchant' is probably the most straightforward, I think."

The handsome young man with lowered eyes – Nicola Suwen – introduced himself as such.

Subaru's eyes widened at the opponent who uttered the family name Suwen, which sounded familiar to his ears. But as if to spur on his surprise and confusion, he didn't stop.

"I'm sure you're surprised by this suddenness, but while you can hardly move your body right now, I'll sadly give you even more shocking news. ――Approximately four hundred years have passed since you were sealed by the hand of the 'Traitor,' Aldebaran."

――――.

――――――――.

――――――――――――.

"――. ――――. ――――――Ah?"

"Four hundred years. Do you understand? You... no, you and Beatrice-chan have awakened four hundred years after your own era. Also, I'll tell you this as well."

Understanding simply couldn't keep up.

Subaru, overwhelmed and swallowed not by the quantity but by the quality of the information. Before such a Subaru, the handsome young man who had caused such an incredible torrent – Nicola, who shared traits with a well-known friend – continued.

It was――,

"――You've kept us waiting far too long, Natsuki-san."

It was a friend's exasperated reprimand, delivered across four hundred years and several lifetimes in between.

