Still, for someone who had until recently been throwing all his energy into the Royal Selection contesting that very kingdom's throne, the news that it had been destroyed was not easily digestible.

"Some things change with the flow of time. Some things don't, ya know. Whatever you find value in, it's foolish to just be swept away and regret it, ya know."

That might have been advice or a warning from an ancient dragon-man who, despite his youthful appearance, had lived alongside humans for over four hundred years, watching their ways.

Even Madelyn and Arakiya, or even Rosalind, the emperor of Vollachia which had swallowed the three nations to become an even greater superpower, could not stop the flow of time.

That was precisely why he thought she was advising him not to simply and obediently go with the flow.

In any case――,

"――I'll... do it."

"That's the spirit, I suppose. Betty will support Subaru with all her might, I wonder."

Time was precious. No matter how much time one had, it was never enough.

No matter how much you value it, what slips through your fingers like grains of sand can never be returned to your hand. So, while it is still in your hand, you must act.

So that you don't realize how fortunate you are only after losing it.


