There, ■■■ paused and gave a chillingly bewitching glance. That it wasn't a movement motivated by positive emotion was clear from the Red Scorpion, which, like Beatrice at Subaru's side, never left her side. The Red Scorpion kept its compound eyes gleaming sharply, as if trying to protect the 'Witch of Melancholy,' who should be inviolable, from all calamities.

"...Were you asked by someone to protect ■■■?"

"...Why do you ask?"

"Just a guess. My memories are tattered, but I thought it would be nice if that were the case."

"You've been... no, from the start, I haven't understood a thing you've said. You and the kid with you are both strange old geezers."

Whether it was a mix of dissatisfaction, displeasure, incomprehension – still low-energy, but those few words, now slightly tinged with emotion, nonetheless struck Subaru sharply.

With the hand not holding Beatrice's, Subaru stroked his completely white hair,

"Being treated like a strange old geezer stings. I still feel young at heart, but I guess that's no good. I even tried to trim my beard like this... respecting my idol, Wilhelm-san."

"Betty thinks any Subaru is handsome... though it's hard to sum up in one word, and it's not an appeal that works for everyone, I suppose."

"Thanks for that praise that didn't quite manage to be reassuring!"

It wasn't exactly something he could be honestly happy about, but he had no doubt there was no lie in it. Otherwise, she couldn't have spent the forty years preparing to accomplish what they had to do – never leaving his side, continuously supporting him. He couldn't find any answer other than love, and he didn't need to.

"Love, huh. Yeah, that's right. That's the only reason to keep going."

"You..."

"It was long, forty years. But even that is one billion, two hundred sixty-two million, two hundred seventy-eight thousand, eighty seconds. Only one-tenth of the time ■■■ spent. Really... really."

The authority of the 'Witch of Melancholy' – even with that power of 'Compression,' as deduced by Beatrice, the time he had actually experienced couldn't fill the gap. The four hundred years ■■■ lived, the days of hell Subaru spent tormented by self-blame and self-punishment – such a span of time that one would want to sneer at it – had worn down ■■■'s heart.

"How did you wear yourself down that much, pay that much of a price for everything, dedicate possibilities to that extent, and still end up here?"

"What are you..."

"Why, ■■■... ■■■!"

"Stop it! Stop calling me that name I can't make out!"

Suddenly, the 'Witch of Melancholy's' expression crumbled, and she stepped back sharply. Still reflexively raising her right hand, ■■■ prepared to snap her fingers and activate her authority. The 'Witch of Melancholy's' authority that never kills, that drives away opponents by manipulating their perceived passage of time――,

"Do it. Try 'Compressing' me."

"――Tch, don't say it so easily. You don't seriously think you can endure it, do you? That's impossible. Anyone who could endure this isn't human. Four hundred years is a long time."

"I know, I suppose."

"――――"

"Betty knows. The four hundred years ■■■ spent and the four hundred years Betty spent are different, but still, I know the loneliness that surely has the same parts, I suppose."

Beatrice, too, had spent an enormous amount of time in the 'Forbidden Library.' And she knew that those empty days, which seemed as if they would never end, did end, and there came a day of liberation.

"Betty wants ■■■ to understand that, I suppose. You have the right to receive it, I wonder. ...No, I want you to receive it, I suppose."

"...Why?"

Hesitating whether to point her poised finger at Subaru or Beatrice, the 'Witch of Melancholy,' revealing an emotion she had never shown before, asked. The sad 'Witch' who, in the process of throwing everything away, had been forced to let go even of reasons.

"Because we want you to be happy. All of us."

"Everyone...?"

"I, Natsuki Subaru."

"Betty, Beatrice, I suppose."

"Emilia," "Frederica," "Otto," "Garfield," "Rem," "Ram," "Roswaal," "Ryuzu," "Meili," "Spica," "Annerose," "Clind," "The people of Arlam Village," "The people of Costuul," "Family," "Companions," "Us," "Betty and the others," "「Everyone」"

"――Tch"

Catching her breath, ■■■'s cheeks stiffened. Not one of those names likely meant anything to ■■■. He understood why. Like Subaru, ■■■ herself, if she stopped thinking about them for even a second, forgot everyone connected to her. Repeating that, she had worn everything away.

"Honestly, when Subaru said he'd just keep thinking about ■■■ forever in some corner of his head, even I thought that was crazy, I suppose."

"Yeah? It's no big deal. Just dedicating one part of my head to ■■■."

"That's how it is, I suppose."

Nodding to each other, they then looked again at ■■■, her eyes fierce. Subaru and the others had answered her 'why.'

Now it was――,

"Now you answer. Answer the 'why' from before."

"The 'why' from before..."

"Why did ■■■ endure four hundred years of emptiness, becoming a 'Witch,' being called a calamity, protecting this place from so many people, I wonder?"

"――――"

At Beatrice's simplified question, ■■■ caught her breath and fell silent. Facing that, Subaru took a step forward. Releasing Beatrice's hand, her small hand gently pushed Subaru's back. One step, one step forward. The distance between him and ■■■, who had stepped back, closed.

"――――Tch"

The Red Scorpion cut in between Subaru and ■■■. As if determined to protect ■■■ from any and all calamities that would harm her, even at the cost of itself.

But――,

"Thanks for doing what we couldn't, all this time."

"――――"

Saying that, as Subaru stroked its carapace, its raised pincers lowered, and with sluggish movements, the Red Scorpion yielded the path to Subaru. At the Red Scorpion's action, ■■■'s eyes widened as if betrayed. ――That was an honor. If she felt the Red Scorpion moving aside was a betrayal,

"For you, me doing this actually means something."

"Ah..."

■■■'s eyes wavered at Subaru, now standing directly in front of her, within arm's reach. Beautiful, his faded, disappearing memories of ■■■ – compared to her in those memories, the woman before him was much more mature, her beauty more striking than any cuteness. The way she chose and wore her dress, her hair styled – even though she showed it to no one, her taste was a bundle of fashion, so typical of ■■■. Even after four hundred years, she hadn't changed those parts, unchanging. That was――,

"Because you wanted to see us – to see me."

"――Ah"

A raspy breath was the final resistance from the 'Witch of Melancholy,' feared throughout the world.

"――――"

With his outstretched hand, Subaru drew her slender body close and embraced ■■■ to his chest. With a start, ■■■'s body trembled as if frightened. But ■■■, heated, did not try to push away Subaru's aged body, which would easily shatter if pushed. Yet she did not embrace him back. That wasn't her rejection――,

"That too, I offered up."

Even the right to embrace someone – she had offered that up, longing for this future. Why? Why had she done it? The answer could only be pressed by Natsuki Subaru. That she had endured four hundred years of emptiness because she wanted to see Natsuki Subaru. And that now, that emptiness – the long, four hundred years of emptiness – was ending.

"I, I, am..."

"It's fine. If you can't embrace anyone, then I'll just embrace you."

"――――"

"If you can't call out names, I'll call out yours. If you can't cry in front of others, I'll let you press your face against my chest like this. If you can't eat the things you like, I'll make you new things you like, as many as you want. If you can't hold anyone's hand, I'll place my hand over yours. If you can't show your weakness to anyone, I'll praise your strength for four hundred years' worth."

What he could do, what he wanted to do, the future, hope, possibilities. The qualification to become the 'Witch of Melancholy' had taken so many things from ■■■. To gain, to grasp those possibilities, she couldn't even wish for them herself.

But――,

"Is it alright, ■■■? Subaru is a genius at arbitrarily worrying about others, arbitrarily imagining their feelings, and arbitrarily trying to make them happy, you know."

"And that's how he talked Betty into it too. ■■■, you become his prey as well."

"――Tch"

Subaru gently lifted the embraced body and looked closely at her surprised face. Despite the emotions welling up inside her, there were no tears in her eyes. Even the right to cry in front of someone was no longer in her hands. What possibilities, hopes, futures remained for her? At least, she hadn't offered up the right to look at him with flushed cheeks and moist eyes.

"This doesn't make sense. You, all of you, don't make sense."

The 'Witch of Melancholy,' captured by a mere human, let that slip in a trembling voice. The 'Witch' who could compress any calamity, pain, or suffering into an instant, her lips trembling as if praying that she would never, ever lose or let go of this single moment.

"It doesn't make sense... but still..."

The 'Witch of Melancholy,' the 'Witch,' ■■■, smiled with moist eyes. As if confirming the emotions surging within her, the ones she hadn't let go of.

"――I think I love you. Strange, right?"

"No? Not at all."

"I suppose."

Had she been prepared for rejection? The love she uttered, accepted without a moment's hesitation, made ■■■'s eyes widen. That face, utterly lacking in 'Witch'-likeness, like a simple village girl, brought a smile to his lips.

"That's way too beautiful for a village girl, though."

"...You probably say that to everyone."

"Even if I did, it's only for village girls too beautiful to be village girls. I don't think there are many candidates. In my experience, just one."

"I see. ...Well, that's fine then."

Hearing Subaru's answer, ■■■ turned her face away in a sulky manner. Finding her cute, Subaru exhaled deeply,

"Hey, can I put you down? My back is kind of killing me."

"You're not saying I'm heavy, are you?"

"No! You're not heavy at all, ■■■, you're like dandelion fluff! But I'm a sixty-year-old geezer! I'm not decrepit, but even being generous, I'm a geezer!"

"Mmm... fine."

Having obtained her consent, he slowly set ■■■ down on the spot. Immediately, Beatrice rushed over and popped into Subaru's arms instead. Seeing that, ■■■'s eyes narrowed again,

"So she's allowed, but I'm not?"

"■■■, you can see for yourself, right? Our Betty is a spirit, true dandelion fluff."

"I'm dandelion fluff, I suppose."

"Perfect sync... fine, whatever."

Turning away from Subaru and Beatrice, ■■■ slowly walked over, stroked the back of the small Red Scorpion at her side, and quietly accused it, "Traitor."

Then, glancing towards the legendary fierce battle that had continued even during this exchange,

"It's gotten really dangerous all of a sudden, but you wanted my help, right?"

"Yeah. We want Veig to behave himself here for a long time. And even after that, there are a lot of things I want to borrow your power for..."

"Planning to use me conveniently? The type who doesn't feed the fish they've caught?"

"I'm the type who wants to say 'I love you' every single day, if possible."

"I see. ...Well, then I won't expect it."

Waving her hand lightly, her reddish-brown hair and large ribbon swaying on her back, ■■■ prepared to leap into the battlefield with the Red Scorpion. Subaru, narrowing his eyes at that ribbon – so familiar, stimulating his memories –,

"――Pe■■!"

"――――"

"Deep inside this glacier, there's another girl I love. Will you help me dig her out later!?"

"Go die, idiot!"

Whether she was serious or not, ■■■ said that, stuck out her tongue, and headed to the battlefield. Scratching his head at that,



